Z||000000||wreakhavoc||03-25-2001||03:28 PM||||I started up my Fiero this morning, shifted into the reverse position and the car moved forward like in 1st gear.  All other gears are working normal.  I drove it yesterday and it worked fine.  The shifter goes into the reverse position as normal but is actually shifting into 1st gear<BR>instead of reverse.<BR>Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||c m west||03-25-2001||04:49 PM||||sounds like you need a new shift select cable<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||03-25-2001||05:46 PM||||On the 4 speed tranny (v6) I thought there was a nut ON the tranny selector for the left right motion shifter cable...  You may just need to adjust this nut as it may have slipped...<BR>I think I had it slip once and I only had reverse first and second till I pulled over and fixed that.<P>Hopefully this is the case so you dont need to buy a new cable, or go rummaging through a boneyard (I think those cables are rather pricey)<P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">  <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||1
